  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_024 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.629 acc. RNA is the dominant signal (rna_only 0.485 vs image_only 0.208), yet we have only ever tested pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder. This is the largest unexplored design dimension. Question: Does a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) outperform PCA in the current best multimodal/multiprofile/avgpool/concat/ViT setting? This experiment isolates exactly one variable (RNA encoder) relative to config_024, giving a clean comparison. Why best next: If scvi_n200 improves, it validates learned RNA encoders and motivates further testing of scgpt; if it does not, PCA suffices and we can focus budget on fusion/aggregation refinements. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty on the most impactful untested axis, making it the highest-information experiment under the limited budget."
